NAME
       vigenere - the classic Vigenere letter cipher (Cyber Range)

SYNOPSIS
       vigenere -k WORD [-d] [FILE]

DESCRIPTION
       The Vigenere cipher moves each letter of a message on through the
       alphabet by the matching letter of a key word (a moves 0 places, b 1,
       c 2 ... z 25), using the key word's letters in turn and starting again
       at its first letter when they run out. Upper and lower case are kept;
       spaces, digits and punctuation pass through unchanged and don't use up
       a key letter. With one key letter it is simply a Caesar shift.

       vigenere reads FILE or standard input and writes the result. Without -d
       it encrypts; with -d it decrypts (moves each letter back).

       Without the key word the cipher is much harder to read than a Caesar
       shift, so the key word is usually the real secret: look for it nearby.

       vigenere is a Cyber Range practice tool; it works only inside the range.

OPTIONS
       -k WORD, --key=WORD
              The key word (letters only; other characters are ignored).

       -d, --decrypt
              Decrypt instead of encrypt.

EXAMPLES
           echo 'attack at dawn' | vigenere -k lemon
           vigenere -d -k lemon message.txt

SEE ALSO
       tr(1), rev(1)
